<article class="env-proposition" id="00OQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00OQ">Proposition <span data-tag="00OQ">10.114.2</span>.</a> A polynomial algebra in $n$ variables over a field is a regular ring. It has global dimension $n$. All localizations at maximal ideals are regular local rings of dimension $n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/00OP" data-tag="00OP">10.114.1</a> all localizations $k[x_1, \ldots , x_ n]_{\mathfrak m}$ at maximal ideals are regular local rings of dimension $n$. Hence we conclude by Lemma <a href="/tag/00OE" data-tag="00OE">10.110.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>